WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.649 --> 00:00:06.209
In this video, we'll review some best practices for organizing your Unreal Engine project.

2
00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:12.699
Despite Unreal Engine 5 introducing a large open-world concept with world partition,

3
00:00:12.699 --> 00:00:18.300
for smaller levels like this one, a persistent level with sublevels is still recommended.

4
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.980
A persistent level often persists throughout the entire game session,

5
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:27.739
while sublevels are children of the persistent level and can be turned on and off or streamed

6
00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:31.579
or unstreamed as needed throughout a project. So in the persistent level,

7
00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:36.380
we mostly try to keep everything that is going to persist throughout the entire project,

8
00:00:36.939 --> 00:00:41.899
key lights for example, cameras, any kind of environmental assets, and then anything that

9
00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:46.619
only needs to come up as needed throughout the project, we'll put those on sublevels and

10
00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:51.020
bring those in only as needed. In the case of this project, we're actually quite comfortable

11
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:57.149
keeping all of it entirely in the persistent level. When organizing your content browser,

12
00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:01.950
be sure to use folders as a way to structure the different needs of the project and do the

13
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.909
same thing in your project outliner, putting key assets in different folders by category,

14
00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:11.549
which can then be toggled on and off even at the outliner level without having to put them

15
00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:17.790
into separate sublevels. A nested folder structure is often recommended, folders inside folders

16
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:22.909
with parent folders being more broad categories and the nested folders being more specific to

17
00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:28.859
particular needs and subcategories. In the next video, we'll go over some tips and additional

18
00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:33.900
resources you can use as you expand your knowledge of OSC for your own projects.
